  "text": "[warm] Step all the way out with me — you can have this. Four steps — each is exactly what rebuilt the map you saw. [short pause] One. Build the plan with an agent; argue until it survives you. The map rebuild's plan came out at forty-four dependent tasks. [short pause] Two. The agent scaffolds the loop: a ledger — the single source of truth — and a workflow that reads it. Then it stops. Nothing runs until you've read what it intends. [short pause] Three. Run it. A worker wakes, does one task, returns a small report. The orchestrator verifies independently — re-runs the gates, never trusts the claim — writes the ledger, picks the next task. The ledger is why an interrupted run resumes cold, without losing a step — it happened during the rebuild, more than once. [short pause] Four. Watch it from outside, the way I watch the estate. Sow a bug. Throttle it. Pause it. The overcrowded manor you saw was healed exactly that way: a bug sown from outside, fixed by the loop. [pause] Two lines are wall-mounted in the skill. One guards the return channel — metadata and pointers, never a payload. The other guards the stop: don't lower this bar, or the loop turns into a chat. [short pause] Brandon has a terminal on the real ledger. Watch one round.",
